other buses, during rush hour traffic in the South Korean city of Seongnam, just south of Seoul.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Former Malaysian leader Najib Razak returns home under royal pardon, but faces a separate 15-year prison sentence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9b83f5ff2da0193272b790691b2640a1f9e7c608306ca79d0b13da3b763550a</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/former-malaysian-leader-najib-razak-returns-home-under-royal-pardon-but-faces-a-separate-15-year-pri/a-79913437--5df11bf7bdda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/former-malaysian-leader-najib-razak-returns-home-under-royal-pardon-but-faces-a-separate-15-year-prison-sentence/a-79913437?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Najib Razak has left prison under a royal pardon, prompting a minister to resign in protest. Malaysia's former leader still faces a separate 15-year sentence over the corruption scandal that brought him down.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan watches for signs of change in Trump's foreign policy priorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54c364d4d8b8341a3a462e678b0ab6e79691d0d9d7318364bd960445c0a788ae</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398--c0dcb3ef3493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tokyo fears the drubbing US President Donald Trump suffered in last week's midterm election may push him to pursue a diplomatic quick win at the expense of Washington's allies in the Indo-Pacific.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: Sonia Gandhi's memoir 'Belonging: A Journey of Love' released</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a07adf901d327ef31248cbbd1919d5f62b113fd9be225a2e8cdec8b9865a37a6</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-sonia-gandhi-s-memoir-belonging-a-journey-of-love-released/a-79908336--355cb9c7bbe4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-sonia-gandhi-s-memoir-belonging-a-journey-of-love-released/a-79908336?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The book goes through the Italian-born matriarch's journey with one of India's most politically influential families. It has already garnered political controversy, with the ruling BJP accusing her of "whitewashing."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: New Delhi ready to mediate Black Sea food corridors, says Ukraine's Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:493010413b98016de27494eabba6e7bedd5d192563557d1efaefd20db929d6e2</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-ready-to-mediate-black-sea-food-corridors-says-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/live-79906023--cfcf53dfd0a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-ready-to-mediate-black-sea-food-corridors-says-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/live-79906023?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said he discussed establishing "food corridors" in the Black Sea in a phone call with Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia shareholders sue Jensen Huang over alleged spy ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad8effaba1aabb1eda8abfe750cb9fe3ef11c659cc2025ac4a00cf5cf664ea35</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-shareholders-sue-jensen-huang-over-alleged-spy-ties/a-79905809--f4200acf2967.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-shareholders-sue-jensen-huang-over-alleged-spy-ties/a-79905809?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia shareholders have sued the chipmaker and its CEO, Jensen Huang, over his alleged ties to a suspected Chinese spy. The case adds to scrutiny over whether sensitive information at the AI giant was compromised.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's demonetization: 10 years on, economic benefits still disputed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dce68e99ebf9ea713ab693a8b88ea43d2a1b4e67651b0a14c66447fc41b5226</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331--2fc450e61f09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the 2016 currency ban, its impact on India's economy and the fight against black money remains contested.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'No choice but to bear it': Delhi's unrelenting air pollution crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13585655ca57fd0a73bc41af6a3cb21b46e7bd0376c12a288b6df7fbb5a73b2c</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124--aa42da1e16d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite years of government interventions, emergency restrictions and public outrage, Delhi continues to battle dangerously polluted air every winter. Why isn't there a lasting solution to a predictable crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02cc59e70ebebd98bbea286f5220e6bfcd25278e40bf5bf3d48cc22e763eda</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>8 ways the US midterm election could affect Donald Trump's Iran policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32e88a8b9031df3fcd76a56a87501df645c286f38c6d0c75aa425b089fa4bb4</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816--8cf7f9243f7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the US midterms could open a window for diplomacy with Iran, they could also unleash a new military escalation. DW spoke with analysts to identify eight factors that could tip the balance toward war or peace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02c897b1188dc56aa7635610b875c9a6ec585de865ac3bece95dbfaf201a41db</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a3279be22e5c6655d8f26cb67f0f70830893102ef42aad04dae0645476771f4</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e62592511b46894eb26c331111da9f059d08e18d792f188df6932faa2edbf0f</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
